262
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,156
( knock at door )

263
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:58,199
Who is it?

264
00:10:58,241 --> 00:10:59,493
Gavin.

265
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:01,328
I brought you
some soup.

266
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:02,621
Why?

267
00:11:02,661 --> 00:11:04,080
Uh, uh, I heard
you were sick.

268
00:11:04,122 --> 00:11:05,081
Oh, right.

269
00:11:05,123 --> 00:11:06,791
Yeah. Hold on,
let me just clean up

270
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:08,084
in here a little bit.

271
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:20,763
( weakly ):
Hello, Gavin.

272
00:11:21,556 --> 00:11:23,642
I missed you at work today.
How you feeling?

273
00:11:23,682 --> 00:11:25,477
I'm not going
to lie to you.

274
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:28,355
I'm pretty sick.

275
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:31,024
Oh, good, because I was having
a totally paranoid moment

276
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:33,360
where I thought
you called in sick to avoid me.

277
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:35,778
Oh, no, no, no, no.

278
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,696
( coughs )

279
00:11:37,738 --> 00:11:38,697
No.

280
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:41,326
So... I had fun last night.

281
00:11:41,368 --> 00:11:44,078
So did I.

282
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:49,417
Exactly how contagious
is this thing you have?

283
00:11:49,459 --> 00:11:51,752
I mean, is it a cold
from standing on the balcony

284
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:54,339
or did a monkey bite ya?

285
00:11:54,381 --> 00:11:56,257
It's just a cold.

286
00:11:56,299 --> 00:11:57,884
You have a fever?

287
00:11:57,925 --> 00:11:59,052
Let me see.

288
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,012
Mm.

289
00:12:01,054 --> 00:12:02,096
Mmm...

290
00:12:05,308 --> 00:12:06,267
Um...

291
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:07,852
What? What is it?
What's the matter?

292
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:10,146
What's Ross doing
to you in that picture?

293
00:12:10,188 --> 00:12:14,275
Oh, he's dusting me
with a fossil brush.

294
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,736
He thought
it would be funny.

295
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:19,030
Right.

296
00:12:19,072 --> 00:12:20,365
Right.

297
00:12:20,407 --> 00:12:21,491
Ross.

298
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:22,617
Yeah.

299
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:24,077
So what's the deal
with you guys?

300
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,246
I don't want to get
in the middle of anything.

301
00:12:26,287 --> 00:12:27,997
Oh... you're not.
You're not.

302
00:12:28,039 --> 00:12:29,874
You're not getting in
the middle of anything.

303
00:12:29,916 --> 00:12:31,585
Don't worry about Ross.
Really, really...

304
00:12:31,626 --> 00:12:32,586
Oh, hide!
That's Ross.

305
00:12:32,627 --> 00:12:34,588
Hide.

306
00:12:34,629 --> 00:12:35,796
Hide, hide.

307
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:36,923
Yeah, but you said
not to worry about...

308
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:38,633
I lied, and I'm not sick either.

309
00:12:38,675 --> 00:12:40,134
Just stay behind the curtain!

310
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:45,181
Hi.

311
00:12:45,223 --> 00:12:46,349
Oh, Molly.

312
00:12:46,391 --> 00:12:48,059
You're not Ross.

313
00:12:48,101 --> 00:12:50,353
No. I'm here to take Emma
to your mother's, remember?

314
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:52,146
Right.
Yes, yes.

315
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,065
Don't panic.

316
00:12:54,107 --> 00:12:55,108
What?

317
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:57,485
There's a man behind
your curtain.

318
00:12:57,527 --> 00:12:58,737
I have mace in my purse...

319
00:12:58,777 --> 00:12:59,946
No, that's okay,
that's okay...

320
00:12:59,987 --> 00:13:01,197
No, no, no, no, no, no.

321
00:13:01,239 --> 00:13:02,616
This is my business
associate Gavin.

322
00:13:02,657 --> 00:13:04,075
He's just being silly.

323
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:05,993
Gavin, come out from behind
the curtain, you silly...

324
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:08,455
Hi.

325
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:10,998
Gavin.
Pleased to meet you.

326
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:14,377
It was my idea
to stand there.

327
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:15,462
Well, hello.

328
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,631
I'll, uh, I'll just
go get Emma.

329
00:13:17,672 --> 00:13:18,965
Okay.

330
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:20,925
( clears throat )

331
00:13:20,967 --> 00:13:23,386
So, um...

332
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:24,803
why did I have to hide?

333
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:26,473
I thought it was Ross.

334
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:27,848
So what if it was?

335
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:30,226
I thought there was nothing
going on between you two.

336
00:13:30,268 --> 00:13:31,311
There isn't.

337
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:32,771
There totally isn't.

338
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:35,189
You hear keys in the hall and
you jump like a young bronco

339
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:37,191
coming out of the chute
for the first time.

340
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:41,571
I used to be
a rodeo clown.

341
00:13:41,613 --> 00:13:43,406
Wow.

342
00:13:43,448 --> 00:13:44,823
Uh, all right, look.

343
00:13:44,865 --> 00:13:47,201
Gavin...

344
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:49,329
I...

345
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:53,082
I guess I-I felt guilty
that you were here.

346
00:13:53,124 --> 00:13:55,502
Which I shouldn't.

347
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:58,338
You know, Ross and I are
not in a relationship.

348
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,297
But...

349
00:13:59,339 --> 00:14:01,675
he is the father of my child.

350
00:14:01,716 --> 00:14:05,136
And you know, we-we
do live together

351
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:07,972
and plus there's just
so much history, you know?

352
00:14:08,014 --> 00:14:10,266
It's just...
I, I don't know.

353
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:11,225
I'm sorry.

354
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,727
I-I'm just all
over the place.

355
00:14:12,769 --> 00:14:14,312
It's okay.

356
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:16,981
Now, I know it's probably
not my place,

357
00:14:17,023 --> 00:14:18,775
but can I give you
a piece of advice?

358
00:14:18,817 --> 00:14:20,109
Yes.

359
00:14:20,151 --> 00:14:22,195
I think you should talk
to Ross about all this.

360
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:26,991
People keep saying that.

361
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:29,868
Oh, I'm sorry, Gavin.

362
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:31,663
Don't be.

363
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:34,165
It's just bad timing.

364
00:14:34,207 --> 00:14:35,709
Mm.

365
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:38,127
So seriously, rodeo clown?

366
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:41,589
One of the best, ma'am,
one of the best.

367
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:46,135
( piano playing
"We Are the Champions" )

368
00:14:46,177 --> 00:14:48,012
♪ No time for ♪

369
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:54,143
♪ Losers, 'cause we
are the champions ♪

370
00:14:54,977 --> 00:15:02,527
♪ Of the world! ♪

371
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:10,993
Oh, she's my
girlfriend.

372
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:13,204
That's not just
how we do it here.

373
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:15,998
Uh, all right, I'm going
to take a little break

374
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,500
and, uh, when we come back,

375
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:20,127
we've got Kenneth
singing "I Touch Myself."

376
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:23,381
I'm not here to judge.

377
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:26,593
( giggles )

378
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:28,052
Oh, you have got to sing.

379
00:15:28,094 --> 00:15:29,929
No, I told you I can't.

380
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:31,347
But you would have so much fun!

381
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:33,683
And you have
a really nice voice.

382
00:15:33,725 --> 00:15:35,602
When have you heard me sing?

383
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:37,478
All the time
when you're cooking.

384
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:38,688
What?

385
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:40,189
Yeah, you're always singing

386
00:15:40,231 --> 00:15:42,316
"Yummy, yummy, yummy,
I've got love in my tummy."

387
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:45,319
Yeah, I do rock that one.

388
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:49,198
Okay, so isn't there
just a little part of you

389
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,617
that wants to get up there?

390
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:52,034
Oh, just a little.

391
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:54,621
But it's just,
God, it's so scary.

392
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:56,955
I mean, I don't even know
what I would sing.

393
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,499
Well, I've got a book around...

394
00:15:58,541 --> 00:16:00,084
"Delta Dawn."

395
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:11,471
Hi. I, uh, I couldn't help
but notice, uh, but that's

396
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:13,807
that's an unusual necklace.

397
00:16:13,848 --> 00:16:17,101
You already hit on me
an hour ago.

398
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:19,270
Right.

399
00:16:19,312 --> 00:16:21,021
So that's a firm no.

400
00:16:28,028 --> 00:16:29,864
I don't believe this.

401
00:16:29,906 --> 00:16:30,990
I just keep striking out.

402
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:33,992
I don't get it either.

403
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:36,329
I mean, you're obviously
desperate.

404
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:39,081
You're asking women
how they want to be killed.

405
00:16:40,792 --> 00:16:42,042
Oh, this is great.

406
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:44,044
Rachel's going
to keep kissing guys

407
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:45,964
until she find
the one she wants,

408
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,841
and I'm, I'm going to die alone.

409
00:16:47,882 --> 00:16:49,634
By drowning, or...

410
00:16:52,219 --> 00:16:54,806
Why would he break up with me?

411
00:16:54,848 --> 00:16:56,474
Oh, I don't know, sweety.

412
00:16:56,516 --> 00:16:59,226
All I ever wanted
was to just love him

413
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:01,187
and have him
love me back.

414
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:03,857
I mean, am I
so unlovable?

415
00:17:03,898 --> 00:17:05,023
( sobs )

416
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:06,526
Wow.

417
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:08,402
I know!

418
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:17,745
( piano plays ending flourish)

419
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:19,163
MIKE:
All right.

420
00:17:19,205 --> 00:17:20,707
That was Kenneth

421
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:24,377
with his much too literal
rendition of "I Touch Myself."

422
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:29,507
Coming up next, we've got Monica
singing "Delta Dawn."

423
00:17:29,549 --> 00:17:30,717
Oh, wait, wait.

424
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:32,385
I can't sing in front
of all these people.

425
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:34,178
Well, just pretend
they're not even here.

426
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:35,471
It's okay.

427
00:17:35,513 --> 00:17:36,723
Monica, once that
spotlight hits you,

428
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,892
it's so bright, you
won't see anyone anyway.

429
00:17:38,933 --> 00:17:40,100
Oh...

430
00:17:42,269 --> 00:17:44,146
Hi, I'm Monica

431
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:47,149
and I'm going to be singing
"Delta Dawn."

432
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:51,153
( applause )

433
00:17:52,697 --> 00:17:54,198
Ooh!

434
00:17:56,701 --> 00:18:03,081
♪ Delta Dawn, what's
that flower you have on? ♪

435
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:11,424
♪ Could it be a faded rose
from days gone by? ♪

436
00:18:11,465 --> 00:18:13,009
Can you totally see
through her shirt?

437
00:18:13,051 --> 00:18:14,301
Like an X ray.

438
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:16,429
( men cheering and applauding )

439
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:19,599
Bad day not to wear a bra.

440
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:26,814
♪ ...Take you
to that mansion in the sky ♪

441
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:28,649
♪ She's 41, and... ♪

442
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:32,152
Hey.

443
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:34,154
I need your help.

444
00:18:36,783 --> 00:18:38,618
Wow, it seems serious.

445
00:18:38,659 --> 00:18:41,829
What seems to be
the problem, Ashley Judd?

446
00:18:42,789 --> 00:18:45,165
Okay, look-- I'm getting
new headshots taken, all right?

447
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:46,793
So I went to get
my eyebrows shaped....

448
00:18:46,834 --> 00:18:47,835
I'm sorry.

449
00:18:47,877 --> 00:18:49,754
Moment to make fun
of that, please.

450
00:18:49,796 --> 00:18:52,924
Okay, I may be a sissy, but I'll
still pound you into the ground.

451
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:55,802
Okay, all right, look.

452
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:57,011
It hurt so bad,

453
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:58,930
I could only let her do
one eyebrow and now...

454
00:18:58,972 --> 00:19:01,849
they don't match!

455
00:19:08,815 --> 00:19:11,191
Huh?

456
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:17,490
It's like a baby caterpillar
chasing its mama.

457
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:18,532
All right,
all right, look.

458
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:20,158
You've got to help
me out, okay?

459
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,744
Look I have a
magic marker.

460
00:19:21,786 --> 00:19:23,162
I want you to fill
in the skinny one

461
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:24,497
so I don't look stupid
for my pictures.

462
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:26,499
Okay, first of all,
this is green.

463
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:27,583
Oh!

464
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:29,335
Well, what the hell
am I supposed to do?

465
00:19:29,376 --> 00:19:31,045
All right, I will
help you out

466
00:19:31,087 --> 00:19:32,463
but you have to promise me

467
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:35,675
you will not tell anyone
what I am about to tell you.

468
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:37,217
What?
What?

469
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:39,846
Okay.

470
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:41,848
You know how most kids
get their allowance

471
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:45,309
from mowing the lawn or
taking out the garbage?

472
00:19:45,351 --> 00:19:49,229
Well, I earned mine by
plucking the eyebrows

473
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:52,191
of my father and his...

474
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:54,318
"business partners."

475
00:19:55,111 --> 00:19:58,238
( laughs )

476
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,198
Oh, my God.

477
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:04,203
Yeah, well, I guess you don't
need my help, Victor/Victoria.

478
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:05,621
Okay, all right,
no, no, no, I do.

479
00:20:05,663 --> 00:20:07,206
I do. I do.
I need your help.

480
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:09,876
But, Chandler, I don't know
if I can take any more plucking.

481
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:11,293
It hurt so bad.

482
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:15,381
Oh, not with my combination
of ice cubes, aloe vera,

483
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:16,423
and my gentle...

484
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:20,260
self-loathing touch.

485
00:20:22,055 --> 00:20:31,438
♪ To take you to that mansion
in the sky! ♪

486
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:34,901
( disappointed groans )

487
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:36,903
I'm sorry.

488
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:38,320
The song's over.

489
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,114
( disappointed groans )

490
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:42,075
Did you see me
up there?

491
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:43,743
Every little
bit of you.

492
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:45,912
Oh! I, I can't believe I did it!

493
00:20:45,953 --> 00:20:48,664
I can't believe I sang in front
of people and they liked me.

494
00:20:48,706 --> 00:20:51,167
Hey, did you hear that one guy
shouting "Look at those tips"?

495
00:20:51,209 --> 00:20:53,878
I mean, did I really help you
get a lot of tips?

496
00:20:55,755 --> 00:20:56,923
Sure.

497
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,382
Wow.

498
00:20:58,424 --> 00:20:59,675
Okay, Mon.

499
00:20:59,717 --> 00:21:02,136
Not that you didn't
sound good...

500
00:21:02,178 --> 00:21:03,345
Good?
Didn't you hear them?

501
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:05,598
I was great!

502
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:07,474
Oh, thank you so much
for making me do this.

503
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:10,519
That is the best gift ever.

504
00:21:10,561 --> 00:21:13,731
Also good gift--
underwear.

505
00:21:16,859 --> 00:21:19,779
Thank you so much
for letting me do this.

506
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,447
Public bathrooms
freak me out.

507
00:21:21,488 --> 00:21:24,033
I can't even pee,
let alone do anything else.

508
00:21:24,075 --> 00:21:29,455
But what's great is you
don't mind talking about it.

509
00:21:29,496 --> 00:21:31,373
God, it's so amazing
that I met you

510
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:33,626
on the same day that Eric
broke up with me,

511
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:37,130
'cause it's, like, you lose a
boyfriend, you get a boyfriend.

512
00:21:37,171 --> 00:21:39,215
Uh-huh.

513
00:21:39,257 --> 00:21:40,340
Look, no, no, no.
Don't worry.

514
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:42,051
This is not some
rebound thing.

515
00:21:42,093 --> 00:21:44,386
I am totally over Eric.

516
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:46,680
Phew!

517
00:21:48,182 --> 00:21:50,601
Okay.

518
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:53,353
Good choice, Ross.

519
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:56,565
Oh, hey!

520
00:21:56,607 --> 00:21:57,942
Hi.
There you are.

521
00:21:57,984 --> 00:21:59,986
I've been looking for you
everywhere.

522
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:00,987
Oh, yeah, hello.

523
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:01,988
Well, here, here I am.

524
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:03,156
Hey, listen, my mom

525
00:22:03,197 --> 00:22:04,949
is not bringing the baby
back until 9:00.

526
00:22:04,991 --> 00:22:07,701
So I was hoping you and I could
have a chance to kind of talk...

527
